        {
            "_id": "hOkfh02TI5JUhAw5",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Tracking Crystal",
            "sort": 1000000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>After the xiomorn trooper deals damage with a crystal shard Strike, a glowing green crystal embeds itself in the target's body. The crystal sheds dim light for 10 feet. While a creature has at least one crystal embedded in its body, all xiomorn troopers gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to [[/act seek]] the creature and to Survival checks to [[/act track]] the creature. In addition, all xiomorn troopers gain a +1 circumstance bonus to attack rolls against the creature. A creature can Interact to remove all tracking crystals embedded in themselves or an adjacent creature.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-effects.Item.Effect: Tracking Crystal]</p>"
                },
